=====================================
FOLDER: NNP_LFER_choice
SYSTEM: MareNostrum 5 — glogin2
CREATED: 29/07/2026
UPDATED: 07/10/2026
PURPOSE: Committee-consistency check on the ArcaNN NNP triplet before committing
         it to production LFER/PMF work: the same reactant->TS1 umbrella-sampling
         PMF is rebuilt three times, each time driven by a different committee
         member.
=====================================

29/07/2026

o Consistency check on the ArcaNN iteration-004 NNP committee before committing to
  it (or its iteration-005 successor, see '../LFER_3_mg2/NNP/') for production
  LFER/PMF work. The same reactant->TS1 umbrella-sampling PMF is reconstructed
  three times, each time using a different one of the three committee members as
  the sole driving potential. The other two are still listed, but only to report
  the model-deviation diagnostic: DeePMD-kit's LAMMPS plugin drives the dynamics
  with the first-listed graph. See 'NNP/README'.

o 'NNP/'         the shared graph triplet.
  'NNP_1/'       PMF driven by graph_1 -- see its README.
  'NNP_2/'       PMF driven by graph_2 -- see its README.
  'NNP_3/'       PMF driven by graph_3 -- see its README.
  'WHAM_files/'  shared WHAM scripts; the result of each arm is the
                 'average_pmf.png' inside the corresponding 'NNP_N/'.

o Comparing 'NNP_1/average_pmf.png' against 'NNP_2/' and 'NNP_3/' is the test:
  if one committee member disagrees enough with the others, the committee has not
  converged for this reaction coordinate and the production pipelines in
  '../LFER_3_mg2/pph4/' should not be trusted yet.

01/10/2026

o Checked the replica layout under each arm. Every 'NNP_N/rep_M' carries the full
  100 umbrella windows, and the per-replica file sets agree once the SLURM job id
  embedded in the 'LAMMPS_DeepMD.<jobid>_<window>' log names is normalised away.
  The replicas are therefore genuinely consistent and are described here once
  rather than in nine separate READMEs. The leftover differences are incidental
  working files that happen to sit in one replica and not another
  ('generate_US_windows.py', 'plumed_USW_XX.dat', 'safe/', a stray 'CV1'), none of
  which affect the sampling.

o Three anomalies that are worth knowing before reading the comparison, because
  they make the three arms unequal:

    'NNP_1/rep_2' is incomplete. It has 1317 files against 1521 in rep_1 and 1512
    in rep_3, and it is missing the window-generation script and the 'safe/'
    backup. Treat the NNP_1 arm as weaker-sampled than the other two.

    'NNP_3/rep_1' contains three FILES literally named 'rep_1', 'rep_2' and
    'rep_3', each 4993 bytes, sitting next to the window directories. They are
    not replica folders. They look like the output of a redirection that was meant
    to go elsewhere, and a script that globs 'rep_*' one level too deep will pick
    them up.

    'NNP_1/rep_3' contains a nested directory also called 'rep_3', holding seven
    stray 'LAMMPS_DeepMD.41690933_*' logs and nothing else. Same cause, same
    hazard.

o None of the three anomalies were modified; they are recorded here only so the
  comparison is read with the right caveats.

07/10/2026

o This is now the only copy of this tree. '../../Train_PPiMg2/NNP_LFER_choice' is a
  symlink pointing here, kept because 1830 files in this tree hardcode that absolute
  path. Editing through either spelling edits the same file.

o Two of the three anomalies recorded on 01/10 are resolved. The three files named
  'rep_1', 'rep_2' and 'rep_3' sitting inside 'NNP_3/rep_1/' are gone: they were
  byte-identical copies of 'job-array_lammps-deepmd_explore_gpu_alogin1.sh', which
  already sat properly named in that same directory, so nothing was lost. The nested
  'NNP_1/rep_3/rep_3/' directory is also gone; none of its eighty 'inputs/' files were
  missing from the parent 'inputs/', and the one template that differed was kept as
  'NNP_1/rep_3/inputs/plumed_USW_XX.dat.from_nested_20260729'.

o The third anomaly stands: 'NNP_1/rep_2' still holds 1317 files against 1521 in
  rep_1 and 1512 in rep_3. That is under-sampling, not clutter, so it was left alone.
  Keep treating the NNP_1 arm as weaker-sampled when comparing the three PMFs.
